From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AppSandbox contributors <appsandbox@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: opt-in native shared ring for the Mutter probe

This patch is for the isolated experiment only.  It is deliberately gated by
ASB_MUTTER_D3D12_SHARE_SOCKET and is not used by appsandbox-display.

Hook points:

  * d3d12_context::fb.cbufs[0] is the currently bound Gallium color target;
  * d3d12_flush() is called by the opt-in Mutter post-paint hook after the
    stage view has been painted and before the native backend presents it;
  * the producer records a GPU-only CopyResource from that actual target into
     three D3D12_HEAP_FLAG_SHARED resources retaining the source DXGI format,
     then signals a producer
    fence through SetEventOnCompletion(eventfd).

No mmap, glReadPixels, PRIME, DMA-BUF, CPU pixel copy, or shared fence is used.
The consumer receives the resource and ready event descriptors with SCM_RIGHTS
and opens the resources on an independent D3D12 device.

The probe currently uses `gpu_copy=1` because the D3D12 driver owns the shared
ring while Mutter owns the render target.  This is the explicitly allowed
second-priority path; the direct shared render-target path remains a separate
optimization after this evidence is collected.

